"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it names (T21.5, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"draft-ietf-oauth-client-id-metadata-document"},{"text":"). # Why this is one nested","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"policy rather than nine fields Every field here is a term of a single decision — ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"do we"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fetch a stranger’s URL and make a client out of what comes back"}]},{"text":" — and none of them means","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anything without [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]. A tenant that states a CIMD posture states all of it; a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant that states none inherits its organization’s whole posture rather than half of one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is the only merge that cannot produce a combination neither party wrote. # The two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fields that can widen, and the seven that cannot [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::allow_http","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"ordered","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": a tenant may turn either off but never on, exactly as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"dynamic_registration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" may only move down its ladder. Everything else names ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this tenant’s"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"domains or ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this tenant’s"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" bounds, and there is no sense in which one tenant’s list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trusted publishers is stricter than another’s — the same argument [","type":"text"},{"code":"OidcPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] already","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes for ","type":"text"},{"code":"dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". # Every bound here is a security control","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::max_metadata_bytes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::min_cache_secs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::max_cache_secs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tuning knobs. They are, respectively, the ceiling on a read from an attacker-chosen URL, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"floor under how often that read may be repeated, and the ceiling on how long its result may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be trusted. Each is clamped again in code against the three constants above, so a settings","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row written by hand cannot lift them.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CimdPolicy"}],"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CimdPolicy"}],"title":"CimdPolicy","roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK10CimdPolicyV","symbolKind":"struct"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy"]}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CimdPolicy/allowHttp":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CimdPolicy\/allowHttp","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"allowHttp","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"allowHttp","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy\/allowhttp","abstract":[{"text":"Permit an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http:\/\/"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"text":" and an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http:\/\/"},{"text":" fetch. ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Development only, and it does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"more than its name says."}]},{"text":" AXIAM’s shared SSRF guard couples the scheme rule to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"address rule — the same seam that lets an integration test point a fetch at a loopback","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mock server — so a tenant that allows ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http"},{"text":" also allows the first hop to resolve to a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"private address. Redirect hops are validated strictly whatever this says, and a public","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deployment that sets it has removed the control that makes ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"169.254.169.254"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unreachable.","type":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CimdPolicy/maxCacheSecs":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CimdPolicy\/maxCacheSecs","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxCacheSecs","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"maxCacheSecs","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy\/maxcachesecs","abstract":[{"text":"The ceiling on a document’s cache lifetime, in seconds. Clamped to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CIMD_MAX_CACHE_CEILING_SECS"},{"text":"].","type":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CimdPolicy/confidentialOnly":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CimdPolicy\/confidentialOnly","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Refuse a document whose "},{"code":"token_endpoint_auth_method","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"none","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Off by default, because","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"none"},{"type":"text","text":" is what every MCP desktop client is. A tenant that turns it on accepts only"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"private_key_jwt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" documents, which is the posture for a deployment whose CIMD clients","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are servers rather than desktops.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"confidentialOnly","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"confidentialOnly","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy\/confidentialonly"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CimdPolicy/trustedRedirectDomains":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The hosts a document’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"redirect_uris","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" may point at, as globs. The loopback hosts","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"127.0.0.1"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[::1]"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localhost"},{"type":"text","text":") are always allowed, because RFC 8252 §7.3 is how"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every desktop MCP client receives its callback — so an empty list is not a refusal of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"everything, it is “loopback only”, which is exactly the Claude Code and VS Code profile."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"trustedRedirectDomains"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"]?"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"trustedRedirectDomains","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy\/trustedredirectdomains","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CimdPolicy\/trustedRedirectDomains"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CimdPolicy/restrictSameDomain":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CimdPolicy\/restrictSameDomain","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"restrictSameDomain","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"restrictSameDomain","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy\/restrictsamedomain","abstract":[{"text":"Require every ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"redirect_uris"},{"text":" host in the document to equal the host of the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"URL itself. ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On by default"}]},{"text":", because the document says who the client is and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"redirect to somewhere else is the one thing a stolen or mirrored document would want to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change. It is turned ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"off"}]},{"text":" for the desktop MCP clients, whose callbacks are on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"loopback and therefore can never share a host with a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https:\/\/"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"text":";","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"docs\/admin\/client-id-metadata-documents.md"},{"text":" says so and says why.","type":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CimdPolicy/enabled":{"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy\/enabled","kind":"symbol","title":"enabled","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CimdPolicy\/enabled","abstract":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Off unless somebody turns it on","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (I1). With this "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a URL-shaped "},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly today’s unknown client: nothing is fetched, nothing is materialised, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ordinary repository lookup answers as it always has."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"enabled"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CimdPolicy/trustedClientIDDomains":{"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy\/trustedclientiddomains","kind":"symbol","title":"trustedClientIDDomains","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CimdPolicy\/trustedClientIDDomains","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The hosts whose documents this tenant will fetch at all, as globs ("},{"code":"mcp.example.com","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"*.example.com","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for every host under one domain). "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An empty list resolves nothing"}]},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and enabling CIMD while it is empty is refused — see ["},{"code":"validate_cimd_policy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]. That is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deliberate departure from “a URL is a client identifier, so any URL will do”: the fetch"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is triggered by an unauthenticated request naming the URL, so an unrestricted list is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request-forgery primitive offered to strangers, bounded only by the SSRF guard’s address"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rules. Naming the publishers a tenant actually fronts costs one settings field and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"removes the class. "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is refused here, and so is a wildcard over a whole top-level"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"domain"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"*.com","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"): both are the posture the empty list is refused for, spelled"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"differently, and a control with no second control behind it cannot have a one-character"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bypass and still be the control. It is a floor and not a public-suffix check —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"*.github.io","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" passes, and trusting shared hosting stays the operator’s decision, bounded"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by the per-tenant quota rather than by this field. "},{"code":"*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" remains valid in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"c